  "route": "Known H=1 uses original round8b; known H=7 uses native TimesFM3 uni21 plus only DEV-selected seven-day residual. This is one routing procedure with two branches, not one identical neural network. Routing never inspects future truth.",
  "training": "Reuse audited native672 forecasts origins7..21. DEV fitting only target dates<14; final only target dates<22, inverse repeated-target-date weights. Existing full-intercept heads reused under same cutoffs; twelve new zero-intercept Ridge configurations fit only native seven-day residuals.",
  "family_selection": "DEV origin14 full7days, fixed candidate blend .25. Prefer nonprior candidates satisfying primary WAPE and daily WAPE<=prior+.001pp, RMSE/P95<=1.005prior, peak<=1.02prior, then most metric-best-control leads and smallest equally normalized primary loss. If none, take minimum-primary-loss nonprior as rejected diagnostic, not adoption.",
  "weight_selection": "DEV origin15 and aggregate origins14/15, both overlapping. For the single family, evaluate common seven-day strengths0/.1/.25/.5/1. Require primary no regression beyond .001pp separately at both origins, RMSE/P95/peak guards, primary improvement>=.001pp on at least one aggregate metric, and aggregate leading metric count>=prior. Select most leads then minimum primary loss, choose smaller weight within one paired-date SE of minimum among same-leading-count eligible strengths. Otherwise keep0. Dates overlap; this is stability screening, not independent confirmation.",
  "frozen_diagnostic": "Always freeze best nonprior family before TEST; diagnostic weight equals selected weight if positive else .25. Only this one diagnostic and frozen selected scheme are TEST-scored. Never reselect after TEST.",
